    - target: {fileID: 2113875699234556495, guid: 18470d71939382448be2ecd06efa9662,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: '<size=42><b>Elastic System Examples</b></size>


        The Elastic
        system allows for dynamic, responsive, and procedural feedback and animations
        within MRTK. The Elastic system is built around a robust damped harmonic
        oscillator simulation system, which is extensible to an arbitrary number
        of dimensions. The output of an elastic system can be used to drive shaders,
        materials, transforms, or pretty much anything your heart desires!


        <b><size="32">Configurability</size></b>

        The
        Elastic system is driven by two pieces of configuration info: the extent
        info and and the properties of the elastic spring itself. The extent of the
        spring can be configured to have defined min/max endpoints and snapping intervals/points,
        and the spring itself can have its mass, input spring constant, end-snap
        spring constant, snapping-interval spring constant, drag/damping factor,
        and the snapping-point radius.


        <b><size="32">Extensibility</size></b>

        The
        base Elastic can be extended to suit several higher-dimensional use cases;
        for instance, instead of using three one-dimensional springs to snap an object
        in 3D space, you can use a three-dimensional spring! And, for rotations,
        you can use a four-dimensional spring to simulate elastic interactions in
        quaternion 4-space. Several of these extensions are included.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
